| * commit 260097b2469918346363bb1c587e1a061c8de8b8 (tooling)
| | Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| | Date:   Thu Apr 30 21:05:18 2026 -0700
| | 
| |     Add cleanliness check + status dashboard (tooling)
| |     
| |     Two more high-leverage scripts on top of build.py + audit_assumptions.py:
| |     
| |     * `scripts/check_cleanliness.py` (~310 lines).  Operationalises the
| |       upstream README "don't be lazy" rule.  For each contender candidate
| |       (configurable list, or supplied as CLI arguments), asks Coq for
| |       `Print T` with `Set Printing All`, recursively up to a configurable
| |       depth, and scans every reachable body for a banned identifier
| |       (`largest_STLCNatRec_nat_of_depth`, `R_tower`, `tPrevMax`, `RT1`,
| |       ...).  Reports each candidate as `clean`, `LAZY`, or `ERROR`.
| |       Heuristic, not a sound transitive analysis -- the depth-2 default
| |       catches every aliasing chain currently in the sandbox; bump
| |       `--depth` if a deeper chain shows up.
| |     
| |       Verified against the current state: `Contender.contender_5` and
| |       every oracle-based sandbox candidate flag LAZY (correctly), the
| |       pure Brouwer-FGH engines (`BigGrow`, `BigGrow_e_omega`,
| |       `BigGrow_pseudo_Gamma_0`) flag clean.  Exit code 1 when any
| |       candidate is lazy, 0 otherwise.
| |     
| |     * `scripts/status.py` (~200 lines).  Thin orchestrator that runs the
| |       three other scripts and stitches their outputs into a single
| |       Markdown dashboard at the repo root (default STATUS.md).  Sections:
| |       build times, Print Assumptions, definition cleanliness, file
| |       metrics (lines, logical name), summary line.  Useful as a relay
| |       snapshot.  STATUS.md added to .gitignore -- it's a derivable
| |       cache, not a tracked artefact.
| |     
| |     Other changes:
| |     
| |     * `.gitignore`: add `/STATUS.md` (anchored to repo root).
| |     
| |     * `scripts/README.md`: describe the new scripts, their flags, exit
| |       codes, extension points, and caveats.  Adjusts the "Why these and
| |       not more" section to acknowledge the four scripts now cover the
| |       high-leverage workflow needs identified in the brainstorming
| |       discussion.
| |     
| |     Engineering details worth recording:
| |     
| |     * Cleanliness check generates one temp `Print T.` script per audited
| |       identifier rather than batching, so a per-Print Coq error (e.g.
| |       identifier not in scope) doesn't poison the whole run.  Fall-back:
| |       silently skip an identifier whose Print fails.
| |     
| |     * The recursion uses Coq's qualified spelling from `Set Printing All`
| |       output, so mid-chain aliases are resolved correctly when fed back
| |       to the next `Print` call.  Without `Set Printing All`, Coq prints
| |       short names that fail to resolve outside the printing module.
| |     
| |     * `status.py` reads `audit_assumptions.py --json` rather than
| |       re-parsing the human-readable Markdown, to keep the join precise.
| |       `check_cleanliness.py`'s output is parsed from Markdown (no JSON
| |       exporter yet); a future change could add `--json` there too.
