* commit 28aa95e856f56f4141c334a7ede34b68fc830591
| Author: Vladimir Reshetnikov <v.reshetnikov@gmail.com>
| Date:   Thu Apr 30 19:39:54 2026 -0700
| 
|     Incorporate review feedback: sharpened don't-be-lazy rule + Approach M
|     
|     The three external reviews in reviews/review-{1,2,3}.md converge on a
|     single major correction to our plan, plus several smaller fixes.
|     
|     ** Strategic correction: definition vs proof **
|     
|     The reviews collectively read the upstream README rule
|     
|       > don't use `contender_N` as a definition when defining `contender_N+1`
|     
|     literally: it forbids using `contender_5` (or its engine) in the
|     contender's *definition*, but says nothing about the *proof*.  Using
|     `contender_5`'s existential maximizer as a *witness* in the proof of
|     strict inequality is exactly the structural-embedding pattern the
|     contest is supposed to reward, and is already the proof shape used by
|     upstream's own `contender_4_lt_contender_5`.
|     
|     This unlocks a much cheaper clean route than the connector lemma:
|     build a fresh-engine `tGrow` shell with no oracle in its definition,
|     extract `t*` for `contender_5` via `Contender.lowerbound_maxBy`,
|     witness `tApp tGrow (tApp tS (embed t*))`.  The contender's
|     definition references only the new language; the proof references the
|     existential witness.  Lower bound is the explicit
|     `BigGrow (S contender_5) <= contender_6` -- a "decisive margin" by the
|     README's own preference.
|     
|     ** Files changed **
|     
|     * AGENTS.md "Current Game Plan": rewritten to make the
|       definition-vs-proof distinction explicit, promote the
|       embedding-witness shell to highest priority, downgrade the connector
|       lemma to "long game", and re-order the candidate directions.
|       Records that this update incorporates review feedback.
|     
|     * IDEAS.md: adds "Approach M -- Embedding-witness fresh-engine shell
|       (NEW, top priority)" as a detailed proof-of-construction sketch for
|       the recommended next experiment (sandbox/GrowEmbed.v in the next
|       session).  Includes the logical-relation proof structure (avoiding
|       FunExt) and a generic Module Type GrowSig refinement.
|     
|     * sandbox/BrouwerHigh.v: Review 1 caught a labeling bug.  The original
|       zeta_0 := epsilon_omega is mathematically wrong (the real zeta_0 is
|       the smallest fixed point of alpha |-> epsilon_alpha, far above
|       epsilon_omega), and the original Gamma_0 needs a real multivariate
|       Veblen function.  Renames the suspect names with a `pseudo_` prefix
|       to flag them as research-grade Brouwer iterates rather than literal
|       ordinal landmarks.  Total Coq functions are unchanged; only the
|       labels and a new explanatory file header.  Print Assumptions still
|       reports closed global contexts for all nine names.
|     
|     ** Other review suggestions noted but not adopted in this commit **
|     
|     * `_CoqProject` / Makefile build harness (Reviews 1, 3): minor
|       hygiene; defer.
|     * Importing coq-contribs/cantor for ordinal/hydra reference (Review 2):
|       adds a heavy dependency; not appropriate for a clean submission.
|     * System F reconnaissance experiment (all three): valuable later,
|       noted in Approach M's "next milestones".
|     * Coq 8.10.2 vs Rocq 9.0.1 compatibility check (Review 1): only
|       relevant once a serious submission candidate exists.
|     
|     The reviews are explicitly not gospel; this commit takes the parts
|     that genuinely improve the plan.
